      "project_id": 34675721,
      "title": "fix(binarymgr): write install progress to stderr",
      "description": "## Description\n\nInstall and download progress from the binary manager (for example the first run of `glab orbit`) was written to stdout. Redirecting a command, like `glab orbit --yes skills get orbit > SKILL.md`, put those progress lines into the output file. Progress and status messages now go to stderr, so stdout carries only the command's own output.\n\n## Related Issues\n\nNo project issue yet.\n\n## How has this been tested?\n\n`go test ./internal/binarymgr/... ./internal/commands/orbit/...` and `golangci-lint run ./internal/binarymgr/...`. The checksum and below-minimum-version tests assert stdout stays empty and the message lands on stderr. A new `HandleInstall` test runs the full download and install against a mocked registry and checks that stdout is empty while stderr has the progress lines.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Agent context</summary>\n\n- `manager.go`: download, checksum, and installed-path messages switched from `LogInfof` to `LogErrorf`.\n- `runner.go`: the custom-binary notice on the run path, the \"No version installed\" line in update, the below-minimum-version warning, and the warning helper also go to stderr.\n- Left on stdout: results of explicit `install`/`update` commands (for example \"already installed\", \"Successfully updated\"), because those are the command's own output.\n\n</details>",
      "state": "merged",
      "created_at": "2026-10-13T12:04:43.342Z",
